===Head to the Seat of Divine Foresight to ask about the situation{{subst:void|<!--102170201-->}}===
{{Mission Description|type=trailblaze|location=Seat of Divine Foresight|After the end of the grand battle against Phantylia, Fu Xuan called for starskiffs and sent everyone back to Exalting Sanctum.<br />However, all of you still struggle to see the full picture behind the rise of the Ambrosial Arbor and the details concerning your time spent on the Xianzhou. Therefore, you all head to the Seat of Divine Foresight to ask for answers.}}
{{Dialogue Start}}
;(По прибытии на место)

;(По прибытии на место)
:Some time later, you arrive at the Seat of Divine Foresight to check on Jing Yuan...
:'''Qingzu:''' Can you wait a little moment? The master diviner will be here soon.
:'''Qingzu:''' She's temporarily taken on the general's responsibilities. Before meeting you, she must make the current situation known and fortify public spirit. This is her first real test as a general &mdash; I hope she can get used to things quickly.
:'''Fu Xuan:''' ...I don't think I can ever get used to this.
:'''Fu Xuan:''' *sigh* It's a pleasure to see you all here today.
:'''Fu Xuan:''' Collating casualties and losses, dispatching forces to round up the remnants of the Disciples, submitting battle reports to the Six Charioteers... Now I know what Jing Yuan meant when he said "the highest throne faces the strongest winds."
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} But you're enjoying yourself, right?
::'''Fu Xuan:''' Generalship is no trifling matter &mdash; how could I be "enjoying myself?" All I can do is get used to it, hmph...
::'''March 7th:''' (I think she's enjoying herself...)
::Share your troubles with me.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Share your troubles with me.
:'''Fu Xuan:''' Generalship is no trifling matter &mdash; it is a duty one must bear.
:'''March 7th:''' (I think she actually really enjoys it...)
:'''Welt:''' Master Diviner, have you summoned us here just to sigh and complain?
:{{tx}}

;(Talk to Qingzu)
;(If {{cx}}<!--performance 102170203 has been seen-->)
::'''Qingzu:''' The Ambrosial Arbor is dormant. Thanks to everyone's hard-fought battles, the Luofu is safe once more.
::'''Qingzu:''' Before he left, the general told me to handle things at the Seat of Divine Foresight. Fortunately, now that victory has been achieved, the plans we prepared will never see the light of day. However...
::'''Qingzu:''' The general did order that if he were unable to return to duty, then the master diviner would take over his duties temporarily.
::{{Диалог|Разговор}} Is the general okay?
:::'''Qingzu:''' Alas, I'm no healer, I'm afraid I couldn't say.
:::'''Qingzu:''' I ordered a military doctor to provide the most comprehensive emergency treatment they could. The Alchemy Commission was caught up in the Sanctus Medicus conspiracy &mdash; it took a lot of work to find someone trustworthy enough to heal the general.
:::'''March 7th:''' If we can help, don't hesitate to ask. I don't know much about medicine, but... there are lots of ways to seal wounds and prevent injuries from worsening.
:::'''Qingzu:''' Don't worry, long-life species are resilient and strong &mdash; the general will pull through. He's faced down situations a hundred times more dangerous than this.
::;(Return to previous option selection)
::{{Диалог|Разговор}} What do you plan on doing with the Ambrosial Arbor?
:::'''Qingzu:''' What do we plan on doing... *sigh* Thousands of years ago, the Xianzhou Alliance was at its wit's end trying to deal with it. Today, nothing's changed.
:::'''Qingzu:''' The Arbor was resurrected. Aside from the Arbiter's Lux Arrow, I'm afraid that nothing can materially harm it. We might be able to suppress it with the help of the Vidyadhara, but with internal strife ravaging their ranks, I'm afraid it's a long shot...
:::'''Welt:''' If you can locate exactly where the Stellaron is within the Arbor, then the Express might be able to help out.
:::'''Qingzu:''' Thank you for your kind offer, Mr. Yang. But something as important and fundamental as the Ambrosial Arbor will require a meeting and deliberation from the Six Charioteers.
::;(Return to previous option selection)
::{{Диалог|Выход}} Fu Xuan seems to be handling things pretty well...
:::'''Qingzu:''' Better to wait until the master diviner has another twenty or thirty years under her belt.
:::'''Qingzu:''' Subduing the enemy is one of the most minor parts of a general's work. They have to meet with the Luofu's Six Charioteers and undergo Ten-Lords Commission inspections &mdash; all while dealing with the Xianzhou Alliance's top brass...
:::'''Qingzu:''' None of it is easy to navigate, but it's a daily responsibility. The crown of a general sits heavy on the head indeed.
:::'''Qingzu:''' I almost forgot &mdash; I need to gather data for the master diviner's draft report. Bye for now.
;(Otherwise)
::'''Qingzu:''' The Luofu's troubles... have only just begun. I don't know if the master diviner can take all this on.

;(Talk to Fu Xuan)
----
:'''March 7th:''' ...Seriously? Thanking us like that, and then immediately sending us on another mission?
:'''Fu Xuan:''' It's not a mission. The Stellaron crisis, the Disciples of Sanctus Medicus rebellion, the Arbor's resurrection, not to mention the Antimatter Legion infiltrating the Luofu... All of these incidents need reporting at the highest level for investigation.
:'''Fu Xuan:''' ...It's just that, having been in the middle of everything, I'm struggling to keep an accurate perspective. I would appreciate if you could go through it all with me, so that I can reacquaint myself with the finer detail.
:'''Fu Xuan:''' So, where should we begin?
:{{Диалог|Разговор}} Let's discuss Phantylia first...
::'''Fu Xuan:''' It appears that Phantylia was the mastermind behind it all. The Xianzhou warred with the Antimatter Legion in the past, and ever since we have kept a watchful eye on their movements.
::'''Fu Xuan:''' Few could have foreseen the insidious tactics employed in the execution of their assaults. The Lord Ravager slithered in unnoticed, clandestinely plotting and machinating, and surreptitiously bestowed a Stellaron upon the Disciples of Sanctus Medicus. This heinous act instigated an uprising aimed at luring the Luofu into a perilous trap of self-destruction.
::'''Fu Xuan:''' The present danger posed by the Legion clearly demands a re-evaluation. We should proceed cautiously.
:;(Return to previous option selection)
:{{Диалог|Разговор}} Let's talk about the Disciples of Sanctus Medicus...
::'''Fu Xuan:''' When the Ambrosial Arbor was severed by the Reignbow Arbiter thousands of years ago, the Abundance became a taboo. Those within the Alchemy Commission &mdash; the original masters of the so-called "way of immortality" &mdash; were ruined at a stroke. The commission became a shadow of its former self.
::'''Fu Xuan:''' Presumably, from that moment on, the seeds of discord for the Disciples of Sanctus Medicus had already been planted... Some of them were willing to work with the enemy, acquiring a Stellaron from the Antimatter Legion to try and revive {{Rubi|the Abundance|Ambrosial Arbor}}.
::'''Fu Xuan:''' Hmm... They succeeded alright, but why would Phantylia's objective be to realize their wishes? Those traitors gained nothing &mdash; they betrayed the Xianzhou only to become sacrificial offerings in the Lord Ravager's grand scheme.
:;(Return to previous option selection)
:{{Диалог|Разговор}} Let's discuss the Stellaron Hunters...
::'''Fu Xuan:''' The Stellaron Hunters? We know just as little. But in the Matrix of Prescience, I saw a prophecy that Kafka received from {{Rubi|Destiny's Slave|Elio}}. Elio foresaw all manner of possibilities for the Luofu...
::'''Fu Xuan:''' Based on what Kafka knows, and despite everything being under the control of Elio, that prophecy is indeed the most beneficial future for the Luofu. The Stellaron Hunters walked right into our trap, and even gifted allies &mdash; in the form of yourselves &mdash; to the Xianzhou... That might sound self-interested, but I hope the feeling is mutual.
::'''Fu Xuan:''' Now that future has come true, the Xianzhou has discovered the Legion's intentions, and with everyone's help, has imposed a crushing defeat on Phantylia.
:;(Return to previous option selection)
:{{Диалог|Выход}} I think we already have the gist...
::'''Fu Xuan:''' That we may, but as logical as things might seem, there are still many details about which we're uncertain.
::'''Fu Xuan:''' For example, how was the Stellaron brought onto the Xianzhou? And who sent it on to Scalegorge Waterscape? How many Disciples of Sanctus Medicus still remain at large? All of this is a mystery. Thus far, we've done our best.
::'''Fu Xuan:''' I'm submitting my written report to the Alliance, and I've already got a plan in mind. All of you will feature in the report, but for the sake of Jing Yuan, anything related to Xianzhou internal affairs will have names redacted &mdash; I hope you can forgive me.
::'''Welt:''' I was about to make the same request, Master Diviner. Since the Arbor's resurrection, I'm sure the Alliance will be poring over every detail of the report. I fear that if the Astral Express gets dragged into matters, leaving will not be an easy task.
::'''Fu Xuan:''' Mm. Jing Yuan has committed quite a few violations this time around, and I'll have to deal with them one by one... *sigh* The Cloud Knight generals are all such a hassle.
::'''Fu Xuan:''' Before you leave, please make time to recuperate. If there's anywhere you'd like to visit, feel free to take a look. I must attend to some Cloud Knight matters &mdash; farewell for now.
::'''Fu Xuan:''' Oh &mdash; if you pass through Starskiff Haven, I have something that I hope you can give to Yukong.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Something Miss Tingyun left behind?
::'''Fu Xuan:''' *sigh* It was all so chaotic. When Phantylia took form, it was as if Tingyun vanished into thin air.
:<pre>{
	"$type": "RPG.GameCore.TalkFigure",
	"ImagePath": "SpriteOutput/Mission/TalkItem/SubMission_140273.png"
}</pre>
::'''Fu Xuan:''' The Cloud Knights were only able to find her fan &mdash; she took it with her everywhere. It's currently unclear if Tingyun was a puppet manipulated by Phantylia, or if some form of deception was used to cloud our vision.
:<pre>{
	"$type": "RPG.GameCore.TalkFigure",
	"Show": false,
	"ImagePath": "SpriteOutput/Mission/TalkItem/SubMission_140273.png"
}</pre>
::'''Fu Xuan:''' I'm already prepared for the worst. Considering how the Legion operates, I fear the fate of the Sky-Faring Commission Amicassador may be a bleak one.
::'''Fu Xuan:''' As for how matters are handled with regards to Tingyun, I believe it's best left to her foxian kin. I have informed the Sky-Faring Commission of the events which took place, and I think it would be best if you were the one to deliver this item to Yukong.
::'''Welt:''' ...I understand. Leave it with us.
::'''Fu Xuan:''' Thank you, Mr. Yang. Now, let me take a look at my remaining duties for the day. *sigh* It's quite the list...
::'''Fu Xuan:''' It's getting late. If you need me, I'll be in the Divination Commission Conclave Hall.
::----

;(Talk to March 7th)
;(If {{cx}}<!--performance 102170207 has been seen-->)
::----
::'''March 7th:''' Well, we had a lot of stumbles along the way, but we still managed to kick butt and save the Luofu without breaking a sweat. Feels kinda surreal.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Maybe this was all fate.
:::'''March 7th:''' (Trailblazer), you don't sound very happy.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} We're just mere puppets of the Stellaron Hunters...
:::'''March 7th:''' Bah, no way! Everything good has come our way due to our hard work. I'm not letting them take any of the credit.
::'''March 7th:''' It may seem like the Stellaron Hunters are controlling everything, but we create our own future. No matter how powerful they are, they can't make a future that doesn't exist come true.
::'''March 7th:''' Since showing up, we've saved a lot of people and averted disaster for the whole Xianzhou. Who cares whether someone or something was directing it? Be happy, (Trailblazer)!
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} What are your plans from here?
::'''March 7th:''' ...Actually, I was wondering if Diviner Fu could do me a favor.
::'''March 7th:''' The Matrix of Prescience has amazing powers, and can iterate and reiterate Kafka's past... So it got me thinking &mdash; if I turned the Matrix on me, could it calculate my past?
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Pretty smart.
:::'''March 7th:''' Hee-hee, yup! When you're free, let's head over to the Divination Commission together and ask them for a favor.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Why didn't you ask Fu Xuan for help while she was here?
:::'''March 7th:''' I was shy! Talking about personal stuff like that in front of everyone... it'd be too embarrassing!
:::'''March 7th:''' When you're free, let's go hit up the Divination Commission together and see what Fu Xuan has to say.
::----
;(Otherwise)
::'''March 7th:''' Here's hoping the Matrix is accurate, and that Diviner Fu won't decline our request...

;(Talk to Welt Yang)
;(If {{cx}}<!--performance 102170205 has been seen-->)
::'''Welt:''' Things have come to a close for now. It's good that you came through unscathed.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Thanks for looking out for me, Mr. Yang.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} What are we going to do next?
::'''Welt:''' The master diviner asked us to pass on this item of Tingyun's. I'll go to the Palace of Astrum and meet with Yukong. If neither of you has anything urgent, it'd be best if you came too.
;(Otherwise)
::'''Welt:''' How am I gonna break this to Madam Yukong...? Maybe she's already heard the news.

;(Talk to Dan Heng)
;(If {{cx}}<!--performance 102170209 has been seen-->)
::----
::'''Dan Heng:''' Returning to the Luofu and Scalegorge Waterscape... it's a surreal feeling.
::'''Dan Heng:''' I left so determined... Who would have thought that circumstances would draw me back once more?
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} It's not like the Xianzhou has done anything to you... yet.
:::'''Dan Heng:''' There are only a handful of individuals who know my identity now. I do not wish to guess what could occur if word gets out.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} How long do you plan on staying here?
:::'''Dan Heng:''' I'll be gone very soon. Jing Yuan is still recovering, and the Cloud Knights won't protect me anymore... It remains to be seen how the Six Charioteers will react to my presence.
::'''Dan Heng:''' But at least for now, I'm safe.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} What are you going to do next?
::'''Dan Heng:''' I want to meet the current high elder of the Vidyadhara.
::'''Dan Heng:''' It seems I won't be able to cast off Dan Feng's negative karma... so I'd like to learn more about his past. I want to find out what I can do to make up for his sins.
::'''Dan Heng:''' If you're planning on an extended stay on the Luofu, I'm afraid I won't be able to join you. I'm sorry, (Trailblazer).
::----
;(Otherwise)
::'''Dan Heng:''' I want to meet the current high elder of the Vidyadhara.
::'''Dan Heng:''' If she can tell me more about Dan Feng's actions, then perhaps I can do something to make up for his sins.
{{Dialogue End}}

